Each manual consists of three sections: General, Product, and Execution.  
- The General section covers universal requirements;  
- The Product section describes specific product needs;  
- The Execution section explains operation and implementation procedures.  

If a project does not require all sections of the Specification, applicable parts can be filtered based on actual needs, compiled into a list, and ultimately formed into the Type of Contents. When using templates, remove non-applicable content, retain relevant sections, and modify or supplement them according to project requirements.  

Items requiring adjustment include project name, date, design phase, etc. The final version must be signed and stamped by an engineer, with a Power Page added. It is recommended to submit all documents as a compressed package.
